### Step 1: Register a New User
# Expected Response: 201 Created
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "don Doe",
  "email": "don.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Step 2: Log In to Get JWT Token
# Expected Response: 200 OK with JWT Token and User Info
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "don.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Automatically capture token in IntelliJ HTTP Client / REST Client
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

###

### Step 3: Get Current User (Fails - No Authorization Header)
# Expected Response: 401 Unauthorized / 403 Forbidden
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me

###

### Step 4: Get Current User (Passes - Dynamic Token Variable)
# Expected Response: 200 OK with User Details
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###

### Step 4 (Alternative): Get Current User (Passes - Manual Paste Token)
# If your HTTP client does not support dynamic variables, paste the token from Step 2 after 'Bearer ' below:
GET http://localhost:8080/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJkb24uZG9lQGV4YW1wbGUuY29tIiwiaWF0IjoxNzg3MDY1MzI5LCJleHAiOjE3ODcxNTE3Mjl9.TmY_BW0qfOrJpFb7IhxU8iYH0Mi4uTufeKLHMLrWy-I
